.agents/skills/manage-asset/SKILL.md:39:2. **Resolve the request** to one procedure (`APR.generate`, `APR.import`, `APR.update`, `APR.deprecate`, or `APR.touch-up`), the kind spec, coverage rules, and asset IDs. If no coverage rule requires the asset, stop: spec first. A new asset's ID comes from `python3 .github/scripts/new_asset_id.py`, used as printed (never typed, copied, or adapted); an update or deprecate reuses the entry's existing ID.
.github/README.md:21:| [`scripts/new_asset_id.py`](scripts/new_asset_id.py) | Generate asset IDs (UUID version 7) per `specs/assets/catalog.md`: the only way to mint one — never type or copy a UUID; `is_asset_id` validates one |
docs/spec-lint.md:32:Asset IDs come only from `python3 .github/scripts/new_asset_id.py`, which mints a UUID version 7 for one new asset: never type, copy, or adapt one, and never reuse a deprecated entry's. `asset_catalog.py` enforces the shape (`I2`); the issuance guidance is [`specs/assets/catalog.md`](../specs/assets/catalog.md) **Asset ID**.
specs/assets/catalog.md:11:- **Asset ID**: a lowercase UUID version 7, such as `0192f3a4-7c1e-7b2a-9d4e-5f6a7b8c9d0e`, generated by `python3 .github/scripts/new_asset_id.py`, never typed or copied. Never changed or reused, including on promotion. Code, catalog cross-references, and issues cite it.
.agents/rules.md:12:- **Aesthetics and assets**: the game's style (medium, pillars, palette, form, motion, interface and sound style) lives in [`specs/aesthetics/`](../specs/aesthetics/aesthetics.md), downstream of definition, quality, design, and view. Asset kinds, tool roles, procedures, style series, and the catalog live in [`specs/assets/`](../specs/assets/assets.md). Identity for a kind uses three pillars: enforced styling (anchors + hard binding or soft exemplars), master/negative `prompt_policy`, and review (look or listen). Visual series use Recraft; music / SFX / voice use the ElevenLabs CLI (SFX soft-enforce until a durable style API exists; never ElevenLabs MCP). Establish or refresh a kind series with `establish-asset-style` (`APR.establish-style`); generate/update/touch-up with `manage-asset`. Most generation tools are Integration ADRs; [`docs/asset-tools.md`](../docs/asset-tools.md) marks Recraft and ElevenLabs ADR-free and **required** for their modality's style-series establish and style-constrained generate; Cheaper Inference is ADR-free for non-series visual generate / reference-anchor (locked steps + `.github/scripts/cheaperinference_image.py`); fal.ai is high-throughput raw image host when the visual series is not `active`. Agent generation is optional. Tools that doc bans (Pixellab) are never used. Catalog person-supplied assets with `register-asset`; review with `review-asset`. Only a person may exempt an asset from review, one at a time, recorded in the catalog. Every asset has a permanent asset ID (UUID version 7 from `.github/scripts/new_asset_id.py`, never typed) and a unique handle `<kind-spec>/<name>`, in one JSON entry file per asset that CI checks (`asset_catalog.py`).
.agents/skills/register-asset/SKILL.md:43:   - **Asset ID**: run `python3 .github/scripts/new_asset_id.py` and use its output. Never type, copy, or adapt a UUID.
